    "title": "Hornets Summer League roster includes former Clemson star, Charlotte native - NewsBreak",
    "text": "CHARLOTTE, N.C. (CAROLINA SPORTS LIVE) — As the Charlotte Hornets continue to make moves in free agency, the team announced its Summer League roster. The roster includes all four new draft picks, plus rostered and two-way players Damion Baugh, Tidjane Salaün K.J Simpson and Charlotte native Jaylen Sims. The rest of the roster is comprised of undrafted free agents, including former Clemson star PJ Hall. Hornets assistant coach Chris Jent will serve as the head coach for the games held July 10-20 in Las Vegas. Joining him on the coaching staff will be Blaine Mueller, Ryan Frazier, Jermaine Bucknor, Kemba Walker, D.J. Bakker and Zeke Chapman. All Hornets Summer League games will be available on the FanDuel Sports Network app. The games will also air on FanDuel Sports Network unless there is a conflict with previously scheduled live event programming. Additionally, all games will be streamed on the Hornets App.\nHornets Summer League Roster (Subject to Change) The Hornets begin Summer League play July 11 against the Jazz. The full schedule can be found here. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Queen City News.",
